            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"A period or place of testing, trials, spiritual darkness, sorrow, or death, often contrasted with mountaintop experiences to represent the low points of human life.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Psalm 23:4\",\"Ezekiel 37:1-2\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"A place of divine judgment, final reckoning, and decision.\",\"basis\":[\"Joel 3:2\",\"Joel 3:14\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"A place of fertility, divine provision, and abundant blessing.\",\"basis\":[\"Psalm 65:13\",\"Deuteronomy 8:7\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"},{\"meaning\":\"The humble or lowly who will be exalted by God's salvation.\",\"basis\":[\"Isaiah 40:4\",\"Luke 3:5\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"},{\"meaning\":\"A place of future hope and restoration born out of trouble.\",\"basis\":[\"Hosea 2:15\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"In popular Christian piety, the valley is most frequently used metaphorically to describe seasons of grief, depression, or spiritual dryness, largely derived from the famous imagery in Psalm 23 of the valley of the shadow of death.\"}",
